[E-PROOF-ONLY] Error: `reify` can only be used in a proof
   ╭─[ reject/reify-test.sw:6:3 ]
   │
 6 │   match reify (() => Fail.need (Some 3) "none") with
   │   ──────────────────────┬─────────────────────  
   │                         ╰─────────────────────── this isn't the body of a proof, so this could run
   │ 
   │ Note 1: `reify` may be used in a `theorem`, or a `def` whose type ends in `Prop` or a type: what it computes is never run
   │ 
   │ Note 2: state what you need as a theorem and use `reify` there; to act on a failure at run time, use a handler such as `Fail.toResult` or `Fail.orElse`
───╯
